  "summary": "Main\nBulkers: Bulker secondhand market activity remained healthy this week, with transactions recorded across a spread of sizes.Appetite from Chinese buyers dominated the week's activity, with Supramaxes proving particularly liquid. Despite uncertainty surrounding the Strait of Hormuz, investor appetite for quality secondhand tonnage has shown little sign of cooling. Values were mixed; firmer pricing drove an upward revision in the Panamax and Handysize sectors, while mid-age Supramax values softened in line with evidence of weaker pricing.",
